  "models": [
    "7M.38"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "findernet.com",
  "description": "Three-phase DIN rail energy meter with Modbus RTU: voltages, currents, powers, power factors, angles, THD, frequency, energy counters, tariffs, identity and communication settings",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Finder, \"Modbus communication protocol 7M24 - 7M38\", v2, 30-06-2021, 7M38 section",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Modbus communication protocol 7M24 - 7M38",
      "version": "v2, 30-06-2021",
      "url": "https://cdn.findernet.com/app/uploads/Modbus-7M24-7M38_v2_30062021.pdf",
      "note": "7M38 section",
      "accessed": "2026-11-14",
      "sha256": "7c7c1fb3c8e2f709ebb755b58069a4a21067f6a1d1c6ef2b6ab3b9f916ecef80"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are register numbers minus 30000 (input registers, FC04) or 40000 (holding registers, FC03/06/16): register 32480 is input address 2480.",
    "This map uses the IEEE 754 float copies of the measurements (32480 onwards); the protocol also has scaled-integer copies (30101-30499) and average, maximum and minimum blocks (35xxx, 36xxx), which are not included.",
    "Energy counters n1-n4 and 1-16 count what their settings select; their unit depends on that setting (Wh, varh or VAh).",
    "Settings that need a password level require the user password written to 40001 first; save them with the operator command (40012 = 1).",
    "The document gives no factory serial settings for the 7M.38.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
